KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Documents the current state of [temp.deduct.funcaddr]: template
argument deduction from the target type of a function-address
context.

CBMC's implementation (added in 18e846497c) handles the std::endl
case where the function parameter is a class-template instantiation
and matching instances can be found in the symbol table.  It does
NOT yet handle the simpler case where the target type is a plain
function pointer with scalar parameter types, as in
  apply(&id_sum, 3, 4)
with
  template <class T> int id_sum(T a, T b);
  int apply(int (*)(int, int), int, int);
The deduction of T=int from 'int (*)(int, int)' falls through to a
"found no match for symbol 'id_sum'" error.
